{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "process-extended-idle-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.42, step 7f: `process-extended-idle`, ATMOSPHERIC CO2 (9090) and Total Energy Consumption (9190) from EXTENDED IDLE for the combination long-haul truck in Washtenaw County at the DEFAULT domain -- the DEFAULT-domain twin of `process-extended-idle-single`, and the only RunSpec here that runs CO2AERunningStartExtendedIdleCalculator on an off-network process. It mounts `moves-onroad.esm`, the DEFAULT domain's catalogue, exactly as `process-tirewear` does: no input database, so every domain-owned table is the default database's -- `hotellingHoursPerDay`, `startsPerDay` and the three hotelling adjustment tables EMPTY, and the input sides of `zoneRoadType`, `zone` and `hotellingActivityDistribution` mounted empty (docs/esm-conventions.md §92-§93). Nothing in the model changed for it.\n\nWHY 9190 IS SELECTED. The fixture asked for 9090 alone and MOVES emitted nothing: CO2AE is chained onto the energy BaseRateCalculator writes, the default emissionRate has no 9090 rows (488 at 9190), and BaseRateGenerator builds base rates only for the selected pollutant-processes. The RunSpec now selects 9190 beside it, as `chain-so2-co2e-mechanism` selects 9101 beside 9001. The 9090<-9190 edge is in no `runspecchainedto` row (0 rows here); the model's CO2AE edge list (`co2aelink_rows`) carries it, and CO2 is energy x carbon content x oxidation fraction x 44/12 per cohort.\n\nWHAT THE DOMAIN CHANGES. hourFractionAdjust is the default hotellingActivityDistribution's at zone 990000, which has a CNG row (mode 200 at 0.80 through model year 2020), so the nine CNG cohorts are 0.8 of the county run's, where Washtenaw's database states no CNG row and MOVES leaves them unscaled. Diesel is the county run's: the county states the default's own daily hotelling total and the default's 990000 mode-200 fractions.\n\n`n_outputRate` IS 100: two blocks of 41 diesel and 9 CNG model years. `run_domainUnported` and `run_selectionUnported` are 0.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
